==Trivia==
*Other than resembling the famously known folktale character [[wikipedia:Little Red Riding Hood|Little Red Riding Hood]], Codename "Red Riding"'s  appearance, personality, and arsenal may be inspired by the ''[[wikia:dark-stalkers:Vampire Savior: The Lord of Vampire|Vampire Savior]]'' character [[wikia:capcom:Baby Bonnie Hood|Baby Bonnie Hood]], who dons an innocent "red riding hood" appearance but in reality is a psychopath. She appears with devilish eyes whenever she is seen attacking, similar to "Red Riding". Hidden in her basket are various weaponry, such as landmines, an Uzi, or, just like "Red Riding", a bazooka.
**The way [[Red Riding Mina (Special Cat)|Awakened Mina]]'s animals cower in fear when Mina is attacking is also reminiscent of how Baby Bonnie Hood's dog Harry cowers in fear when she attacks.
*She uses an exploding [[Doge Dark]] as a rocket, which is replaced by a [[Killer Cat (Rare Cat)|Killer Cat]] when she joins the Cat Army.
*She has the largest blind spot in the game, at 2,800.

